[{"id":"nazara-83-23-2","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"čekaju","en":"they wait"},{"bs":"da pogledamo","en":"so that we may look"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"}],"ref":"83:23","answerWord":"يَنظُرُونَ","answerSound":"audio/7e58c2476b5034bd5986.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"On couches, gazing,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["عَلَى","ٱلْأَرَآئِكِ","يَنظُرُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-37-73-0","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"gledamo","en":"we look"}],"ref":"37:73","answerWord":"فَٱنظُرْ","answerSound":"audio/3600727fc735401235c8.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then see the nature of the consequence for those warned,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["فَٱنظُرْ","كَيْفَ","كَانَ","عَٰقِبَةُ","ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-4-50-0","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pogledaj!","en":"look!"},{"bs":"pogledaj nas!","en":"look at us!"},{"bs":"pa gledaju","en":"so they look"},{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"}],"ref":"4:50","answerWord":"ٱنظُرْ","answerSound":"audio/0d72213facde227b6847.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"See, how they invent lies about Allah! That of itself is flagrant sin.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["ٱنظُرْ","كَيْفَ","يَفْتَرُونَ","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","ٱلْكَذِبَ","وَكَفَىٰ","بِهِۦٓ","إِثْمًا","مُّبِينًا"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-12-109-15","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa gledaju","en":"so they look"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"},{"bs":"pogledaj nas!","en":"look at us!"},{"bs":"pogledaj!","en":"look!"}],"ref":"12:109","answerWord":"فَيَنظُرُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/d9f507b0cf454ab391b9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We sent not before thee (any messengers) save men whom We inspired from among the folk of the townships - Have they not travelled in the land and seen the nature of the consequence for those who were before them? And verily the abode of the Hereafter, for those who ward off (evil), is best. Have ye then no sense? -","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["وَمَآ","أَرْسَلْنَا","مِن","قَبْلِكَ","إِلَّا","رِجَالًا","نُّوحِىٓ","إِلَيْهِم","مِّنْ","أَهْلِ","ٱلْقُرَىٰٓ","أَفَلَمْ","يَسِيرُوا۟","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","فَيَنظُرُوا۟","كَيْفَ","كَانَ","عَٰقِبَةُ","ٱلَّذِينَ","مِن","قَبْلِهِمْ","وَلَدَارُ","ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ","خَيْرٌ","لِّلَّذِينَ","ٱتَّقَوْا۟","أَفَلَا","تَعْقِلُونَ"],"marked":[15],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-27-69-4","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pogledajte!","en":"so (you all) look!"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"},{"bs":"gleda","en":"he/it looks"}],"ref":"27:69","answerWord":"فَٱنظُرُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/9c9482df7191374ed95a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Travel in the land and see the nature of the sequel for the guilty!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قُلْ","سِيرُوا۟","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","فَٱنظُرُوا۟","كَيْفَ","كَانَ","عَٰقِبَةُ","ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-56-84-2","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"da pogledamo","en":"so that we may look"},{"bs":"i pogledaj nas!","en":"and look at us!"}],"ref":"56:84","answerWord":"تَنظُرُونَ","answerSound":"audio/4c0e32dc669624c63f2a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And ye are at that moment looking","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["وَأَنتُمْ","حِينَئِذٍ","تَنظُرُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-3-77-18","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"gleda","en":"he/it looks"},{"bs":"i pogledaj nas!","en":"and look at us!"},{"bs":"gledaju","en":"they look"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"}],"ref":"3:77","answerWord":"يَنظُرُ","answerSound":"audio/d5451dcc43186bb792f1.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah's covenant and their oaths, they have no portion in the Hereafter. Allah will neither speak to them nor look upon them on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He make them grow. Theirs will be a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَشْتَرُونَ","بِعَهْدِ","ٱللَّهِ","وَأَيْمَٰنِهِمْ","ثَمَنًا","قَلِيلًا","أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","لَا","خَلَٰقَ","لَهُمْ","فِى","ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ","وَلَا","يُكَلِّمُهُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","وَلَا","يَنظُرُ","إِلَيْهِمْ","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","وَلَا","يُزَكِّيهِمْ","وَلَهُمْ","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[18],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-6-11-5","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"gledamo","en":"we look"},{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"}],"ref":"6:11","answerWord":"ٱنظُرُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/d8ab3034f6857867e950.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say (unto the disbelievers): Travel in the land, and see the nature of the consequence for the rejecters!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قُلْ","سِيرُوا۟","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","ثُمَّ","ٱنظُرُوا۟","كَيْفَ","كَانَ","عَٰقِبَةُ","ٱلْمُكَذِّبِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-80-24-0","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"gledamo","en":"we look"},{"bs":"gledam","en":"I look"},{"bs":"pričekajte nas!","en":"(you all) wait for us!"}],"ref":"80:24","answerWord":"فَلْيَنظُرِ","answerSound":"audio/5a9bcb3898ed5ccbbb26.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Let man consider his food:","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["فَلْيَنظُرِ","ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ","إِلَىٰ","طَعَامِهِۦٓ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-2-104-7","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pogledaj nas!","en":"look at us!"},{"bs":"gleda","en":"he/it looks"},{"bs":"gledam","en":"I look"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"}],"ref":"2:104","answerWord":"ٱنظُرْنَا","answerSound":"audio/40289b88fffd0af39da2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"O ye who believe, say not (unto the Prophet): \"Listen to us\" but say \"Look upon us,\" and be ye listeners. For disbelievers is a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["يَٰٓأَيُّهَا","ٱلَّذِينَ","ءَامَنُوا۟","لَا","تَقُولُوا۟","رَٰعِنَا","وَقُولُوا۟","ٱنظُرْنَا","وَٱسْمَعُوا۟","وَلِلْكَٰفِرِينَ","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-7-86-19","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"i pogledajte!","en":"and (you all) look!"},{"bs":"pa gledaju","en":"so they look"},{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"}],"ref":"7:86","answerWord":"وَٱنظُرُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/e7bf75f7a792dc3b4063.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lurk not on every road to threaten (wayfarers), and to turn away from Allah's path him who believeth in Him, and to seek to make it crooked. And remember, when ye were but few, how He did multiply you. And see the nature of the consequence for the corrupters!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["وَلَا","تَقْعُدُوا۟","بِكُلِّ","صِرَٰطٍ","تُوعِدُونَ","وَتَصُدُّونَ","عَن","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","مَنْ","ءَامَنَ","بِهِۦ","وَتَبْغُونَهَا","عِوَجًا","وَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟","إِذْ","كُنتُمْ","قَلِيلًا","فَكَثَّرَكُمْ","وَٱنظُرُوا۟","كَيْفَ","كَانَ","عَٰقِبَةُ","ٱلْمُفْسِدِينَ"],"marked":[19],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-7-129-19","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa gleda","en":"so he/it looks"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"},{"bs":"čekaju","en":"they wait"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"}],"ref":"7:129","answerWord":"فَيَنظُرَ","answerSound":"audio/19b8b77c3c426e31894c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They said: We suffered hurt before thou camest unto us, and since thou hast come unto us. He said: It may be that your Lord is going to destroy your adversary and make you viceroys in the earth, that He may see how ye behave.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قَالُوٓا۟","أُوذِينَا","مِن","قَبْلِ","أَن","تَأْتِيَنَا","وَمِنۢ","بَعْدِ","مَا","جِئْتَنَا","قَالَ","عَسَىٰ","رَبُّكُمْ","أَن","يُهْلِكَ","عَدُوَّكُمْ","وَيَسْتَخْلِفَكُمْ","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","فَيَنظُرَ","كَيْفَ","تَعْمَلُونَ"],"marked":[19],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-7-185-1","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"gledaju","en":"they look"},{"bs":"pričekajte nas!","en":"(you all) wait for us!"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"}],"ref":"7:185","answerWord":"يَنظُرُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/527a7a5e1d62f079fcc5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Have they not considered the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and what things Allah hath created, and that it may be that their own term draweth nigh? In what fact after this will they believe?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["أَوَلَمْ","يَنظُرُوا۟","فِى","مَلَكُوتِ","ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ","وَٱلْأَرْضِ","وَمَا","خَلَقَ","ٱللَّهُ","مِن","شَىْءٍ","وَأَنْ","عَسَىٰٓ","أَن","يَكُونَ","قَدِ","ٱقْتَرَبَ","أَجَلُهُمْ","فَبِأَىِّ","حَدِيثٍۭ","بَعْدَهُۥ","يُؤْمِنُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-9-127-4","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"},{"bs":"pa gleda","en":"so he/it looks"},{"bs":"gledaju","en":"they look"}],"ref":"9:127","answerWord":"نَّظَرَ","answerSound":"audio/4e9cf1d97d4728719fd0.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And whenever a surah is revealed, they look one at another (as who should say): Doth anybody see you? Then they turn away. Allah turneth away their hearts because they are a folk who understand not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["وَإِذَا","مَآ","أُنزِلَتْ","سُورَةٌ","نَّظَرَ","بَعْضُهُمْ","إِلَىٰ","بَعْضٍ","هَلْ","يَرَىٰكُم","مِّنْ","أَحَدٍ","ثُمَّ","ٱنصَرَفُوا۟","صَرَفَ","ٱللَّهُ","قُلُوبَهُم","بِأَنَّهُمْ","قَوْمٌ","لَّا","يَفْقَهُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-10-14-7","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"da pogledamo","en":"so that we may look"},{"bs":"pa gleda","en":"so he/it looks"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"čekaju","en":"they wait"}],"ref":"10:14","answerWord":"لِنَنظُرَ","answerSound":"audio/765fdfc33485feeba4cd.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then We appointed you viceroys in the earth after them, that We might see how ye behave.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["ثُمَّ","جَعَلْنَٰكُمْ","خَلَٰٓئِفَ","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِهِمْ","لِنَنظُرَ","كَيْفَ","تَعْمَلُونَ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-27-27-1","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pogledat ćemo","en":"we will look"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"},{"bs":"pogledaj!","en":"look!"}],"ref":"27:27","answerWord":"سَنَنظُرُ","answerSound":"audio/4cbd28e7c751f7f690eb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(Solomon) said: We shall see whether thou speakest truth or whether thou art of the liars.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قَالَ","سَنَنظُرُ","أَصَدَقْتَ","أَمْ","كُنتَ","مِنَ","ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-27-33-9","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"},{"bs":"pogledao je","en":"he/it looked"},{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"},{"bs":"gledaju","en":"they look"}],"ref":"27:33","answerWord":"فَٱنظُرِى","answerSound":"audio/64ef982eb580367bbac8.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They said: We are lords of might and lords of great prowess, but it is for thee to command; so consider what thou wilt command.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قَالُوا۟","نَحْنُ","أُو۟لُوا۟","قُوَّةٍ","وَأُو۟لُوا۟","بَأْسٍ","شَدِيدٍ","وَٱلْأَمْرُ","إِلَيْكِ","فَٱنظُرِى","مَاذَا","تَأْمُرِينَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-27-41-4","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"gledamo","en":"we look"},{"bs":"pogledajte!","en":"(you all) look!"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"gledate","en":"you are looking"}],"ref":"27:41","answerWord":"نَنظُرْ","answerSound":"audio/29eae5da5c061e68c257.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He said: Disguise her throne for her that we may see whether she will go aright or be of those not rightly guided.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["قَالَ","نَكِّرُوا۟","لَهَا","عَرْشَهَا","نَنظُرْ","أَتَهْتَدِىٓ","أَمْ","تَكُونُ","مِنَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","لَا","يَهْتَدُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-37-88-0","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"pa je pogledao","en":"then he looked"},{"bs":"gledam","en":"I look"},{"bs":"gledamo","en":"we look"},{"bs":"pa pogledaj!","en":"so look!"}],"ref":"37:88","answerWord":"فَنَظَرَ","answerSound":"audio/8541e2c2d49db4ea3c02.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And he glanced a glance at the stars","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["فَنَظَرَ","نَظْرَةً","فِى","ٱلنُّجُومِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"nazara-50-6-1","words":["verb:nazara"],"options":[{"bs":"gledaju","en":"they look"},{"bs":"pa neka pogleda","en":"so let him look"},{"bs":"pa je pogledao","en":"then he looked"},{"bs":"i pogledaj nas!","en":"and look at us!"}],"ref":"50:6","answerWord":"يَنظُرُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/521845e500f4244a747c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Have they not then observed the sky above them, how We have constructed it and beautified it, and how there are no rifts therein?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"gledati","en":"to look"},"passage":["أَفَلَمْ","يَنظُرُوٓا۟","إِلَى","ٱلسَّمَآءِ","فَوْقَهُمْ","كَيْفَ","بَنَيْنَٰهَا","وَزَيَّنَّٰهَا","وَمَا","لَهَا","مِن","فُرُوجٍ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"نَظَرَ"}},{"id":"labitha-20-103-3","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostali ste","en":"you stayed"},{"bs":"i ostali su","en":"and they stayed"},{"bs":"(nisu) boravili","en":"they (had not) stayed"},{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"}],"ref":"20:103","answerWord":"لَّبِثْتُمْ","answerSound":"audio/ad05f0d9ff143a6e44eb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Murmuring among themselves: Ye have tarried but ten (days).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["يَتَخَٰفَتُونَ","بَيْنَهُمْ","إِن","لَّبِثْتُمْ","إِلَّا","عَشْرًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-79-46-4","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"(nisu) boravili","en":"they (had not) stayed"},{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"},{"bs":"ostao si","en":"you stayed"},{"bs":"ostao sam","en":"I stayed"}],"ref":"79:46","answerWord":"يَلْبَثُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/29242fbaab1d650dd1a2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"On the day when they behold it, it will be as if they had but tarried for an evening or the morn thereof.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["كَأَنَّهُمْ","يَوْمَ","يَرَوْنَهَا","لَمْ","يَلْبَثُوٓا۟","إِلَّا","عَشِيَّةً","أَوْ","ضُحَىٰهَا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-18-26-4","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostali su","en":"they stayed"},{"bs":"ostao si","en":"you stayed"},{"bs":"ostali ste","en":"you (all) stayed"},{"bs":"ostaju","en":"they stay"}],"ref":"18:26","answerWord":"لَبِثُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/f27bae5fb1499cb77849.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: Allah is Best Aware how long they tarried. His is the Invisible of the heavens and the earth. How clear of sight is He and keen of hearing! They have no protecting friend beside Him, and He maketh none to share in His government.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["قُلِ","ٱللَّهُ","أَعْلَمُ","بِمَا","لَبِثُوا۟","لَهُۥ","غَيْبُ","ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ","وَٱلْأَرْضِ","أَبْصِرْ","بِهِۦ","وَأَسْمِعْ","مَا","لَهُم","مِّن","دُونِهِۦ","مِن","وَلِىٍّ","وَلَا","يُشْرِكُ","فِى","حُكْمِهِۦٓ","أَحَدًا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-12-42-13","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"},{"bs":"i ostao si","en":"and you stayed"},{"bs":"(nisu) boravili","en":"they (had not) stayed"},{"bs":"ostali smo","en":"we stayed"}],"ref":"12:42","answerWord":"فَلَبِثَ","answerSound":"audio/bd5c3411faaaa74fc759.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And he said unto him of the twain who he knew would be released: Mention me in the presence of thy lord. But Satan caused him to forget to mention it to his lord, so he (Joseph) stayed in prison for some years.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["وَقَالَ","لِلَّذِى","ظَنَّ","أَنَّهُۥ","نَاجٍ","مِّنْهُمَا","ٱذْكُرْنِى","عِندَ","رَبِّكَ","فَأَنسَىٰهُ","ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","ذِكْرَ","رَبِّهِۦ","فَلَبِثَ","فِى","ٱلسِّجْنِ","بِضْعَ","سِنِينَ"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-23-113-1","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostali smo","en":"we stayed"},{"bs":"ostao sam","en":"I stayed"},{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"},{"bs":"ostali su","en":"they stayed"}],"ref":"23:113","answerWord":"لَبِثْنَا","answerSound":"audio/1326c5a5d1f4804b9b8e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They will say: We tarried by a day or part of a day. Ask of those who keep count!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["قَالُوا۟","لَبِثْنَا","يَوْمًا","أَوْ","بَعْضَ","يَوْمٍ","فَسْـَٔلِ","ٱلْعَآدِّينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-11-69-10","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostao je","en":"he/it stayed"},{"bs":"ostaju","en":"they stay"},{"bs":"ostali ste","en":"you (all) stayed"},{"bs":"ostali su","en":"they stayed"}],"ref":"11:69","answerWord":"لَبِثَ","answerSound":"audio/009bbf0b7ede20cd1876.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And Our messengers cam unto Abraham with good news. They said: Peace! He answered: Peace! and delayed not to bring a roasted calf.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["وَلَقَدْ","جَآءَتْ","رُسُلُنَآ","إِبْرَٰهِيمَ","بِٱلْبُشْرَىٰ","قَالُوا۟","سَلَٰمًا","قَالَ","سَلَٰمٌ","فَمَا","لَبِثَ","أَن","جَآءَ","بِعِجْلٍ","حَنِيذٍ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-17-76-9","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostaju","en":"they stay"},{"bs":"ostao sam","en":"I stayed"},{"bs":"ostali smo","en":"we stayed"},{"bs":"ostao je","en":"he/it stayed"}],"ref":"17:76","answerWord":"يَلْبَثُونَ","answerSound":"audio/d0d4a983a6aa7eef7340.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they indeed wished to scare thee from the land that they might drive thee forth from thence, and then they would have stayed (there) but a little after thee.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["وَإِن","كَادُوا۟","لَيَسْتَفِزُّونَكَ","مِنَ","ٱلْأَرْضِ","لِيُخْرِجُوكَ","مِنْهَا","وَإِذًا","لَّا","يَلْبَثُونَ","خِلَٰفَكَ","إِلَّا","قَلِيلًا"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-18-12-7","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"ostali su","en":"they stayed"},{"bs":"ostao sam","en":"I stayed"},{"bs":"ostali smo","en":"we stayed"},{"bs":"ostali ste","en":"you (all) stayed"}],"ref":"18:12","answerWord":"لَبِثُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/f411e097646143ed7168.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And afterward We raised them up that We might know which of the two parties would best calculate the time that they had tarried.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["ثُمَّ","بَعَثْنَٰهُمْ","لِنَعْلَمَ","أَىُّ","ٱلْحِزْبَيْنِ","أَحْصَىٰ","لِمَا","لَبِثُوٓا۟","أَمَدًا"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-18-25-0","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"i ostali su","en":"and they stayed"},{"bs":"i ostao si","en":"and you stayed"},{"bs":"(nisu) boravili","en":"they (had not) stayed"},{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"}],"ref":"18:25","answerWord":"وَلَبِثُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/109b7765b14911034127.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And (it is said) they tarried in their Cave three hundred years and add nine.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["وَلَبِثُوا۟","فِى","كَهْفِهِمْ","ثَلَٰثَ","مِا۟ئَةٍ","سِنِينَ","وَٱزْدَادُوا۟","تِسْعًا"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"labitha-26-18-5","words":["verb:labitha"],"options":[{"bs":"i ostao si","en":"and you stayed"},{"bs":"i ostali su","en":"and they stayed"},{"bs":"pa je ostao","en":"so he/it stayed"},{"bs":"(nisu) boravili","en":"they (had not) stayed"}],"ref":"26:18","answerWord":"وَلَبِثْتَ","answerSound":"audio/4e78c4731bcacce00d54.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(Pharaoh) said (unto Moses): Did we not rear thee among us as a child? And thou didst dwell many years of thy life among us,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ostati, boraviti","en":"to stay, to remain"},"passage":["قَالَ","أَلَمْ","نُرَبِّكَ","فِينَا","وَلِيدًا","وَلَبِثْتَ","فِينَا","مِنْ","عُمُرِكَ","سِنِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"لَبِثَ"}},{"id":"faqiha-9-87-10","words":["verb:faqiha"],"options":[{"bs":"razumiju","en":"they understand"},{"bs":"razumijete","en":"you (all) understand"},{"bs":"razumiju ga","en":"they understand it"},{"bs":"razumijemo","en":"we understand"}],"ref":"9:87","answerWord":"يَفْقَهُونَ","answerSound":"audio/d8fad0a95fa6a01036fa.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They are content that they should be with the useless and their hearts are sealed, so that they apprehend not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"razumjeti, shvatiti","en":"to understand"},"passage":["رَضُوا۟","بِأَن","يَكُونُوا۟","مَعَ","ٱلْخَوَالِفِ","وَطُبِعَ","عَلَىٰ","قُلُوبِهِمْ","فَهُمْ","لَا","يَفْقَهُونَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"فَقِهَ"}},{"id":"faqiha-11-91-3","words":["verb:faqiha"],"options":[{"bs":"razumijemo","en":"we understand"},{"bs":"razumijete","en":"you (all) understand"},{"bs":"razumiju","en":"they understand"},{"bs":"razumiju ga","en":"they understand it"}],"ref":"11:91","answerWord":"نَفْقَهُ","answerSound":"audio/8a9df7fce4b7b9c3b4a2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They said: O Shu'eyb! We understand not much of that thou tellest, and lo! we do behold thee weak among us. But for thy family, we should have stoned thee, for thou art not strong against us.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"razumjeti, shvatiti","en":"to understand"},"passage":["قَالُوا۟","يَٰشُعَيْبُ","مَا","نَفْقَهُ","كَثِيرًا","مِّمَّا","تَقُولُ","وَإِنَّا","لَنَرَىٰكَ","فِينَا","ضَعِيفًا","وَلَوْلَا","رَهْطُكَ","لَرَجَمْنَٰكَ","وَمَآ","أَنتَ","عَلَيْنَا","بِعَزِيزٍ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"فَقِهَ"}},{"id":"faqiha-17-44-15","words":["verb:faqiha"],"options":[{"bs":"razumijete","en":"you (all) understand"},{"bs":"razumiju ga","en":"they understand it"},{"bs":"razumijemo","en":"we understand"},{"bs":"razumiju","en":"they understand"}],"ref":"17:44","answerWord":"تَفْقَهُونَ","answerSound":"audio/d7d1d90345a9ad58d87d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The seven heavens and the earth and all that is therein praise Him, and there is not a thing but hymneth His praise; but ye understand not their praise. Lo! He is ever Clement, Forgiving.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"razumjeti, shvatiti","en":"to understand"},"passage":["تُسَبِّحُ","لَهُ","ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ","ٱلسَّبْعُ","وَٱلْأَرْضُ","وَمَن","فِيهِنَّ","وَإِن","مِّن","شَىْءٍ","إِلَّا","يُسَبِّحُ","بِحَمْدِهِۦ","وَلَٰكِن","لَّا","تَفْقَهُونَ","تَسْبِيحَهُمْ","إِنَّهُۥ","كَانَ","حَلِيمًا","غَفُورًا"],"marked":[15],"facts":{"verb":"فَقِهَ"}},{"id":"faqiha-20-28-0","words":["verb:faqiha"],"options":[{"bs":"razumiju","en":"they understand"},{"bs":"razumijete","en":"you (all) understand"},{"bs":"razumijemo","en":"we understand"},{"bs":"razumiju ga","en":"they understand it"}],"ref":"20:28","answerWord":"يَفْقَهُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/8460244461d6bf8030fd.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"That they may understand my saying.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"razumjeti, shvatiti","en":"to understand"},"passage":["يَفْقَهُوا۟","قَوْلِى"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"فَقِهَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-2-127-8","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"prihvati!","en":"accept!"},{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"},{"bs":"prihvaćen je","en":"he/it was accepted"}],"ref":"2:127","answerWord":"تَقَبَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/c687e95f15d5f099870e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when Abraham and Ishmael were raising the foundations of the House, (Abraham prayed): Our Lord! Accept from us (this duty). Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Hearer, the Knower.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["وَإِذْ","يَرْفَعُ","إِبْرَٰهِۦمُ","ٱلْقَوَاعِدَ","مِنَ","ٱلْبَيْتِ","وَإِسْمَٰعِيلُ","رَبَّنَا","تَقَبَّلْ","مِنَّآ","إِنَّكَ","أَنتَ","ٱلسَّمِيعُ","ٱلْعَلِيمُ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-3-35-12","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa prihvati!","en":"so accept!"},{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"},{"bs":"prihvata","en":"he/it accepts"}],"ref":"3:35","answerWord":"فَتَقَبَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/3fa26b9cca5d993f1120.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(Remember) when the wife of 'Imran said: My Lord! I have vowed unto Thee that which is in my belly as a consecrated (offering). Accept it from me. Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Hearer, the Knower!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["إِذْ","قَالَتِ","ٱمْرَأَتُ","عِمْرَٰنَ","رَبِّ","إِنِّى","نَذَرْتُ","لَكَ","مَا","فِى","بَطْنِى","مُحَرَّرًا","فَتَقَبَّلْ","مِنِّىٓ","إِنَّكَ","أَنتَ","ٱلسَّمِيعُ","ٱلْعَلِيمُ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-5-27-9","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa je prihvaćen","en":"so he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"pa prihvati!","en":"so accept!"},{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"},{"bs":"prihvatamo","en":"we accept"}],"ref":"5:27","answerWord":"فَتُقُبِّلَ","answerSound":"audio/759b28e373ab1d469020.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But recite unto them with truth the tale of the two sons of Adam, how they offered each a sacrifice, and it was accepted from the one of them and it was not accepted from the other. (The one) said: I will surely kill thee. (The other) answered: Allah accepteth only from those who ward off (evil).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["وَٱتْلُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","نَبَأَ","ٱبْنَىْ","ءَادَمَ","بِٱلْحَقِّ","إِذْ","قَرَّبَا","قُرْبَانًا","فَتُقُبِّلَ","مِنْ","أَحَدِهِمَا","وَلَمْ","يُتَقَبَّلْ","مِنَ","ٱلْءَاخَرِ","قَالَ","لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ","قَالَ","إِنَّمَا","يَتَقَبَّلُ","ٱللَّهُ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-5-27-13","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"},{"bs":"prihvati!","en":"accept!"},{"bs":"pa je prihvaćen","en":"so he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"}],"ref":"5:27","answerWord":"يُتَقَبَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/a85e5fa315de1d05cb02.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But recite unto them with truth the tale of the two sons of Adam, how they offered each a sacrifice, and it was accepted from the one of them and it was not accepted from the other. (The one) said: I will surely kill thee. (The other) answered: Allah accepteth only from those who ward off (evil).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["وَٱتْلُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","نَبَأَ","ٱبْنَىْ","ءَادَمَ","بِٱلْحَقِّ","إِذْ","قَرَّبَا","قُرْبَانًا","فَتُقُبِّلَ","مِنْ","أَحَدِهِمَا","وَلَمْ","يُتَقَبَّلْ","مِنَ","ٱلْءَاخَرِ","قَالَ","لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ","قَالَ","إِنَّمَا","يَتَقَبَّلُ","ٱللَّهُ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-5-27-20","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"prihvata","en":"he/it accepts"},{"bs":"i primi","en":"and accept"},{"bs":"prihvaćen je","en":"he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"}],"ref":"5:27","answerWord":"يَتَقَبَّلُ","answerSound":"audio/8ed5f4d8935adb1bdafe.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But recite unto them with truth the tale of the two sons of Adam, how they offered each a sacrifice, and it was accepted from the one of them and it was not accepted from the other. (The one) said: I will surely kill thee. (The other) answered: Allah accepteth only from those who ward off (evil).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["وَٱتْلُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","نَبَأَ","ٱبْنَىْ","ءَادَمَ","بِٱلْحَقِّ","إِذْ","قَرَّبَا","قُرْبَانًا","فَتُقُبِّلَ","مِنْ","أَحَدِهِمَا","وَلَمْ","يُتَقَبَّلْ","مِنَ","ٱلْءَاخَرِ","قَالَ","لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ","قَالَ","إِنَّمَا","يَتَقَبَّلُ","ٱللَّهُ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ"],"marked":[20],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-5-36-19","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"prihvaćen je","en":"he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"prihvatamo","en":"we accept"},{"bs":"prihvati!","en":"accept!"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"}],"ref":"5:36","answerWord":"تُقُبِّلَ","answerSound":"audio/278e92367ca2f1c76d80.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"As for those who disbelieve, lo! if all that is in the earth were theirs, and as much again therewith, to ransom them from the doom on the Day of Resurrection, it would not be accepted from them. Theirs will be a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","لَوْ","أَنَّ","لَهُم","مَّا","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","جَمِيعًا","وَمِثْلَهُۥ","مَعَهُۥ","لِيَفْتَدُوا۟","بِهِۦ","مِنْ","عَذَابِ","يَوْمِ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","مَا","تُقُبِّلَ","مِنْهُمْ","وَلَهُمْ","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[19],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-9-53-6","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"},{"bs":"prihvati!","en":"accept!"},{"bs":"prihvaćen je","en":"he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"}],"ref":"9:53","answerWord":"يُتَقَبَّلَ","answerSound":"audio/a85b24511a7e7aaea030.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: Pay (your contribution), willingly or unwillingly, it will not be accepted from you. Lo! ye were ever froward folk.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["قُلْ","أَنفِقُوا۟","طَوْعًا","أَوْ","كَرْهًا","لَّن","يُتَقَبَّلَ","مِنكُمْ","إِنَّكُمْ","كُنتُمْ","قَوْمًا","فَٰسِقِينَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-14-40-7","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"i primi","en":"and accept"},{"bs":"prihvata","en":"he/it accepts"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"},{"bs":"biva prihvaćen","en":"he/it is accepted"}],"ref":"14:40","answerWord":"وَتَقَبَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/bc3ad4bfca0b0f27003c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"My Lord! Make me to establish proper worship, and some of my posterity (also); our Lord! and accept my prayer.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["رَبِّ","ٱجْعَلْنِى","مُقِيمَ","ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ","وَمِن","ذُرِّيَّتِى","رَبَّنَا","وَتَقَبَّلْ","دُعَآءِ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}},{"id":"taqabbala-46-16-2","words":["verb:taqabbala"],"options":[{"bs":"prihvatamo","en":"we accept"},{"bs":"pa je prihvaćen","en":"so he/it was accepted"},{"bs":"i primi","en":"and accept"},{"bs":"pa ju je prihvatio","en":"so he/it accepted her"}],"ref":"46:16","answerWord":"نَتَقَبَّلُ","answerSound":"audio/afee0f616c8742e584b7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they do, and overlook their evil deeds. (They are) among the owners of the Garden. This is the true promise which they were promised (in the world).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"prihvatiti, primiti","en":"to accept"},"passage":["أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","نَتَقَبَّلُ","عَنْهُمْ","أَحْسَنَ","مَا","عَمِلُوا۟","وَنَتَجَاوَزُ","عَن","سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ","فِىٓ","أَصْحَٰبِ","ٱلْجَنَّةِ","وَعْدَ","ٱلصِّدْقِ","ٱلَّذِى","كَانُوا۟","يُوعَدُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"تَقَبَّلَ"}}]